{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update33.json\", \"summary\": \"Interpreted the dedicated PreVote receipt (c72c66880fd9498ca1efb95774b0b06e, experiment 381d89a2) that had been executed but never accounted for: all five comparisons resolved, so the account of Q2 now carries the measured bound that PreVote alone ends the removed singleton leader's window after one heartbeat tick (pre-step-down stale answer at parsed index 3 violated; post-step-down request unanswered at index 5). With that resolved, I also requested the next execution for the remaining discriminator - the forwarded route - as a new self-contained harness (assurance_forwarded_read_test.go) where the requester is the group's learner, its forwarded MsgReadIndex is held across the committed removal of the leader, and the witness is the answer that crosses back to that requester. Two new source ranges (raft.go:1764-1770 the follower forward, raft.go:2072-2087 responseToReadIndexReq) support the request. The harness was built against the captured source and, in a clean copy of the module containing only that file, runs the intended sequence: the learner consumes read index 2 while the actual leader of {2} has committed 4, the removed leader steps down after one tick, and the later request is not answered. Validation reports valid with sources, investigation discriminator, interpretation and experiment effects.\"}"}}
